# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# uv
uv.lock.bak

# CatBoost training-run artifacts (written to cwd by default during .fit())
catboost_info/

# Data / models / state (all reproducible from ingestion; never committed)
data/**
!data/.gitkeep
models/**
!models/.gitkeep
predictions/**
!predictions/.gitkeep
reports/**
!reports/.gitkeep
# Narrow, deliberate exceptions (M17 draft-engine forensic audit): unlike everything else
# under reports/, these two are NOT reproducible from `alpha-squad ingest` -- they are raw
# diagnostic evidence from a specific ~42-minute forensic run, and three tracked documents
# (docs/DRAFT_ENGINE_FORENSIC_AUDIT.md, docs/DRAFT_CONTROLLED_EXPERIMENTS.md,
# docs/DRAFT_ENGINE_REDESIGN_RECOMMENDATION.md) cite them as their evidence base. Ignoring
# them would leave those documents pointing at dangling evidence after a fresh clone.
!reports/draft_decision_trace.json
!reports/draft_forensics_experiment_results.json
# D55 adds two more: the P-tier ablation that chose the shipped formula, and the
# post-implementation re-trace proving the mechanism (not just the roster counts) changed.
!reports/draft_forensics_ptier_results.json
!reports/draft_decision_trace_d55.json
# D58/D60 (1-QB format retarget): the M-tier ablation that chose marginal starter value over
# VORP as the score's value base, and the pick-level counterfactual attribution both
# docs/FORMAT_MIGRATION_DIAGNOSTIC.md (S7-8) and docs/DECISIONS.md D60 cite as their evidence.
# Same reasoning as the M17/D55 exceptions above: not reproducible without redoing the full
# ingest/train/market pipeline, so kept alongside the documents that cite them.
!reports/draft_forensics_mtier_results.json
!reports/pick_attribution.json
# W1.1/D110 (weekly program): the FantasyPros API boards are NOT reproducible from
# `alpha-squad ingest` and, unlike everything else here, cannot be re-fetched at will -- the
# configured key is a public tier (`limit: 10` rows per board) with a request quota that
# exhausted during the harvest. Two tracked documents
# (docs/weekly/W11_FANTASYPROS_FLEX_AUDIT.md, docs/weekly/W2_ECR_BENCHMARK_RESULTS.md) cite
# them as the evidence that a real weekly FLEX board exists and that the mirror reconstruction
# reproduces it. Same reasoning as the M17/D55/D58 exceptions above. Each board carries a
# `content_sha256` so a later re-harvest can be diffed rather than silently replacing this
# vintage. Contains only ranking + player identity: no schedule or roster field is retained,
# because those are not historical in this payload (D110 §3).
# Git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so the directories are
# un-ignored first, then the files inside them.
!reports/weekly/
!reports/weekly/fp_api_cache/
!reports/weekly/fp_api_cache/**
# The W2 benchmark output the results document quotes throughout. Reproducible in principle,
# but only after a full ingest + feature build, and it is the artifact a future phase diffs
# against to check the benchmark has not drifted.
!reports/weekly/w2_results.json
# W3/D111: the Alpha-vs-ECR-vs-baseline benchmark output. Reproducible only after a full
# 2015-2025 ingest, feature build and model training run (~hours); the results document quotes
# it throughout and a later phase diffs against it to check the baseline has not drifted.
!reports/weekly/w3_results.json
state/**
!state/.gitkeep
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Frontend
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Claude Code agent worktrees (isolation:"worktree" sub-agents), never project content
.claude/
